## Why This Is Asked
This question probes end-to-end thinking on governance, data lineage, and drift in a multi-tenant Azure OpenAI deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant policy enforcement and data residency
- Drift detection across prompts and retrieved knowledge
- Data lineage with Azure Purview and observability with Azure Monitor
- PII redaction before OpenAI calls and grounding with Cognitive Search

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(text){
  // naive: redact an email-like token if present
  if (text.indexOf('@') >= 0) {
    const at = text.indexOf('@')
    const left = text.substring(0, at)
    return left + '[REDACTED_EMAIL]'
  }
  return text
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement the drift alert rule and rollback workflow in Azure Monitor?
- What tests would you automate to validate PII redaction and policy gating across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a privacy-preserving, multi-tenant AI workflow at scale, with strict data isolation, governance, and measurable latency.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant OpenAI deployment and prompt routing
- Real-time ingestion (Event Hubs) and low-latency scoring
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search on Blob data
- PII redaction (Text Analytics) and per-tenant masking (Key Vault)
- RBAC (Azure AD), Data Lake auditing, canary rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: route prompt for tenant, redact, ground, respond
async function handleRequest(req){
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const raw = req.body;
  const redacted = redactPII(raw);
  const kb = loadKBVersion(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, kb, tenantId);
  const resp = await openai.complete(prompt, {deployment: getDeployment(tenantId)});
  logAudit(tenantId, prompt, resp);
  return resp;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to quantify latency vs. isolation trade-offs?
- How to implement drift detection for the KB and prompts across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to design scalable, compliant, multi-tenant AI flows in Azure, balancing data residency, prompt governance, and cost.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data residency and isolation
- Prompt versioning and policy gating
- Pluggable grounding knowledge sources
- Canary-style prompt rollouts behind API Management
- Prompt caching and cost controls
- Auditing and telemetry across tenants

